{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgAfwJYkYFM3xkj1GR262","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Audit report — the visible world loads and stays there + off-screen work/loading pressure\n\nScope checked: `src/render/renderPackageLoader.js`, `assetLoader.js`, `partsLibrary.js` (admission/readmission/retry/readiness), `liveGeometryAdmission.js`, `pipelineAutoFlushPolicy.js`, `admissionSliceBudget.js`, `asyncAdmission.js`, `flightReadySet.js`, `entityMeshVisibility.js`, `readyPackagedBodies.js`, `sectorPredict.js`, the renderer's `sector:exit` / `run:ended` / spawn-warm bus wiring, `src/core/presentationAdmission.js`, `src/systems/claims.js`, `src/systems/encounterDirector.js`, `src/main.js` startup gates.\n\nChecked and found clean (stating these so they are not re-audited): the New Game / Continue readiness ladder is **fail-closed, not fail-open** — `flightReadySet.js` `READY_STATUSES` excludes every failure verdict, and each `main.js` gate is timeout-bounded and throws `GameStartReadinessError` into a presenter with a route back. Negative fetch results are not cached (`assetLoader.js:177,189` evict the key), so re-admission genuinely re-fetches. `retryFailedAuthoredAdmission` is driven from the ordinary residency poll (`queueOrRequestAuthoredUpgrade`), is attempt-capped with backoff, and correctly refuses to retry a root that already shows a readable body. The target-lock gate refuses an abstract marker (`presentationAllowsTargetLock` → `presentationFallbackVisible`), so \"empty lock\" is explicitly handled. `authoredOpeningFailedClosed` excluding failure states from `openingPending` is deliberate and does not reach the blocking `FlightReadySet`.\n\n---\n\n### F-LOAD-01\n- symptom: A mission target whose authored hull fails admission can end up permanently drawn as the abstract octahedron and permanently un-lockable — the player cannot target or kill it, so the mission cannot be completed.\n- severity: softlock\n- route: Accept a mission with a required-whole-ship target → the target's authored admission exhausts its retry budget (`AUTHORED_ADMISSION_RETRY_MAX = 4`, ~37 s of backoff) → the mission-critical procedural-fallback thunk is consumed → the thunk throws.\n- owner: `src/render/renderer.js` `syncResolvingMarker` (~:5869–5890); thunk minted in `src/render/visualOverrides.js` `directAuthoredAdmissionSubstrate` (~:795) from `factory.build`\n- evidence: Lines ~5878–5879 `delete parentData.admissionProceduralFallback` run **before** `fallbackThunk()` is invoked at ~5881, and the invocation is wrapped in `catch (_) { /* the marker remains the terminal visual */ }`. On a throw the thunk is already gone, so no later frame can retry it, and `authoredReadableFallbackRetained` / `presentationFallbackVisible` are never set. `src/core/presentationAdmission.js:183-184` then returns `false` from `presentationAllowsTargetLock` for the `unavailable` admission forever, and `src/systems/weapons.js:647` / `src/ui/uiRoot.js:2091,2223` refuse the contact. Retries cannot re-arm it either: `unavailable`/`fallback-after-error` sit outside `READMISSION_STATUSES` (`partsLibrary.js:2773-2783`) and the retry budget is spent.\n- suggested_fix: Delete the thunk only after `fallbackThunk()` returns a usable `Object3D`; on throw, leave it in place and stamp a backoff mark so a later terminal frame re-attempts once, bounded by a small attempt counter.\n- confidence: low (the logic is confirmed; reachability depends on `factory.build` throwing, which is exceptional)\n- note: foreign-lane file dirty — `renderer.js` has uncommitted work, but `git diff -U0` shows its first content hunk at line 11070, so this code is at HEAD and is not another agent's in-flight hunk.\n\n### F-LOAD-02\n- symptom: At the moment a ship's authored body gives up, a freshly built procedural hull pops in and the frame stalls — a shader link and a full vertex-buffer upload land inside the presented frame instead of before it.\n- severity: minor\n- route: Any ship whose authored admission exhausts its retries while on the glass — a combat spawn burst or a sector arrival on a contended/iGPU host is the realistic case.\n- owner: `src/render/renderer.js` `syncResolvingMarker` (~:5881–5886)\n- evidence: The terminal path does `parent.add(fallback)` and nothing else. Compare the renderer's own mount protocol for a newly created root at ~:28566–28576: it tests `hasUnresidentGeometry(m)`, sets `userData.geometryPending = true`, enqueues on `this._liveGeometryAdmissions`, and then calls `compileObjectPipelines(m)`. The terminal publish does none of the four. The parent substrate is already submitted at that point (status is terminal, so `isAuthoredPendingStatus` is false and the `authoredPending` gate in `entityMeshVisibility.js:32` no longer hides it), so the child draws on the next frame uncompiled and un-uploaded — exactly the condition the `pipelinesPending`/`geometryPending` latches exist for (`entityMeshVisibility.js:22-35`). The thunk builds a brand-new graph (`visualOverrides.js:1438-1442` → `factory.build`); the \"programs are already linked\" reasoning that justifies the *pending-window* fallback (`partsLibrary.js:2995-2996`) does not apply here, because that fallback was attached before the boundary ever drew. Several procedural materials are also uncached (`visualFactory.js:618,638,1246,2404`), so a new program permutation is possible.\n- suggested_fix: Route the terminal fallback through the same mount protocol: set `geometryPending` when `hasUnresidentGeometry(fallback)`, `enqueue(entity, fallback)` on the live-geometry lane, and call `compileObjectPipelines(fallback, { debugBy: 'terminal-procedural-fallback' })` before it is allowed to draw.\n- confidence: medium\n- note: foreign-lane file dirty — same as F-LOAD-01; the cited lines are outside every uncommitted hunk.\n\n### F-LOAD-03\n- symptom: When a claim raid is aborted and re-arms, the second attempt's attackers arrive cold — their hulls decode at the spawn instead of during the countdown, so the player sees stand-ins or a hitch at the moment the fight starts.\n- severity: minor\n- route: Fly to a player claim under raid warning → the encounter is admitted and then aborted (`aborted:<reason>`) → the warning re-arms for the reprieve window → the squad fires again.\n- owner: `src/render/renderer.js` `onBus('encounter:resolved')` (~:21329–21331) vs `src/systems/claims.js` `_onDefenseEncounterResolved` (:1729–1734) and `_tickRaidDefenses` (:1662–1674)\n- evidence: The renderer deletes the warm roster on `encounter:resolved` **unconditionally**, with no outcome test. `encounterDirector.js` ~:2311–2320 emits `encounter:resolved` with `outcome: 'aborted:<reason>'` on the abort path. `claims.js:1730-1733` then sets `defense.phase = 'warning'` with an extended `deadlineAt` but never re-emits `claim:defenseWarning` — and `claim:defenseWarning` is the only trigger for `_publishClaimDefenseRoster` other than restore (`encounterDirector.js:362`, `:701-707`). `warmClaimDefenseDecode` (`renderer.js:7302-7315`) therefore finds `defense.phase === 'warning'` but `rosters.get(defense.encounterId)` undefined and warms nothing for the whole reprieve. The same gap exists on the `CLAIM_DEFENSE_TERMINAL_REFUSALS` re-arm at `claims.js:1671`. The spawn kick (`entity:spawned` → `kickSpawnedEntityDecode`) is the only remaining lead, which is what the roster warm exists to pre-empt.\n- suggested_fix: Skip the roster delete when `String(payload.outcome).startsWith('aborted:')`, or have `claims.js` re-emit `claim:defenseWarning` on both re-arm paths so the director republishes the roster.\n- confidence: high\n\n### F-LOAD-04\n- symptom: Nothing visible; a per-run bookkeeping map grows for the life of the page across repeated title → New Game / Continue cycles.\n- severity: polish\n- route: Play a run with claim raids, return to title, start another run, repeat.\n- owner: `src/render/renderer.js` `onBus('run:ended')` (~:21538–21550) and `_claimDefenseRosters` (~:21326)\n- evidence: `_claimDefenseRosters` is pruned only by `encounter:resolved` / `claim:defenseResolved` for a matching `encounterId` (~:21330, :21335). The `run:ended` handler clears every sibling of exactly this class — `_swarmWarmCoveredEnemyIds`, `_swarmWarmReKickClaims`, `_waveHullDecodePending`, `state.render.swarmDeferredWarm` — but not this map. The renderer outlives a run (title → New Game reuses it), so any defense live at run end leaves a permanent entry, keyed `claim-defense:<bodyId>:<seq>` where `meta.nextRaidId` restarts per run.\n- suggested_fix: Add `this._claimDefenseRosters?.clear()` to the existing `run:ended` handler, beside the other warm-bookkeeping clears.\n- confidence: high\n\n### F-LOAD-05\n- symptom: Nothing visible in isolation; on a dense sector arrival the live-geometry lane spends a growing share of its 3 ms slice re-deriving the same camera/glass numbers instead of admitting geometry, so rock and prop bodies take longer to appear under exactly the load the lane is paced for.\n- severity: polish\n- route: Arrive in a belt sector (or any arrival that latches many rocks/props as `geometryPending` at once) and watch the ambient lane drain.\n- owner: `src/render/renderer.js` `priorityOf` passed to `createLiveGeometryAdmissionQueue` (~:14457–14466); scan in `src/render/liveGeometryAdmission.js` `pickNextWhere` (:95–113)\n- evidence: `pickNextWhere` calls `entryPriority` for every entry in `pending` on every pick, and the renderer's `priorityOf` calls `renderAdmissionEnv(state)` *inside itself* (:14460). `renderAdmissionEnv` (:1468–1489) recomputes `glassCornerWu` (trig) and `admissionAnchorPos` on each call; the env is identical for every entry in one pick. Draining n entries is therefore O(n²) env derivations. The queue's re-grade-per-pick is intentional (header comment, lines 6–8), so the fix is the env, not the re-grade. The repo already uses exactly this hoist elsewhere: `queueOrRequestAuthoredUpgrade` takes a `scan` that is \"verdict-identical with player/camera/glass resolved once at pass head instead of per call\" (:4563–4565). Dead entries short-circuit before the env (:14458), so this cost falls on the live-burst case, not on corpses. Separately, `pickNextWhere` never drops entries whose `active()` is already false, and `runEntry` awaits `yieldToMain()` before its first `active()` check (:117–119); the yield is a resolved microtask while the slice has room (`pipelineAutoFlushPolicy.js:125`), so each stale entry costs slice time rather than a present — small, but it is the same fix site.\n- suggested_fix: Give `pickNextWhere` a per-pick context: derive the env once at the top of the scan and pass it to `priorityOf(entity, root, ctx)`, mirroring the existing `scan` parameter pattern. While there, drop entries failing `active()` inside the scan instead of carrying them to a drain turn.\n- confidence: medium\n- note: foreign-lane file dirty — `renderer.js`; line numbers above are working-tree numbers and sit outside every uncommitted hunk (`liveGeometryAdmission.js` and `pipelineAutoFlushPolicy.js` are clean).\n\n---\n\nNot re-reported (already open in the demo defect ledger, §6): D226 (wreck-cathedral LOD1 shell loss), D229 (metallic-rock blink through the rock-family decode rewarm), D199, D130, D224.\n\nVERDICT: 5 findings"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1339,"cache_read_input_tokens":213702,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1339},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c020a9ae-f380-4499-9216-2daa8d6e2392","uuid":"852054c9-182f-4cdb-9c40-7f8f7d89981a","timestamp":"2026-10-19T00:47:04.027Z","request_id":"req_011CgAfwJASDT8B4D83diNwm"}
